OLTP vs OLAP
Primary purpose: 			
OLTP : process operational transactions				
OLAP: analyze data and support decisions

Workload:
OLTP: many short, concurrent read/writes
OLAP: fewer but heavier scans, joins, aggregations

Data:
OTLP: current, detailed operational records
OLAP: historical, integrated, often summarized

Typical Operations:
OLTP: insert, update, delete, point lookups
OLAP: LArge scans, group-by, aggregations, comparisons

Schema:
OLTP: Normalized (usually 3nf) for integrity
OLAP: Often denormalized(Star/snowflake) or wide tables

Storage:
OLTP: typically row oriented
OLAP: typically column oriented

Latency goal: 
OLTP: ms
OLAP: sec


